# LeakSanitizer suppressions for test runs (applied by the default 'asan' test setup in
# tests/meson.build). Keep each rule narrow and say why it is safe.

# OpenSSL's one-time config load during OPENSSL_init_crypto (reached through libcurl's first
# init) allocates per-thread error state that OpenSSL never frees. It is a single 904-byte
# block per process, owned by OpenSSL, and not reachable from YAMS code.
leak:ossl_init_config
